Phase I: Business Process Explanation
Project: SmartHerd: Modern Livestock Management & Veterinary Care System
Student: Aphrodis Senga (ID: 20251SEN137) | Course: INSY 8311 - Database Development
with PL/SQL
1. Business Process Overview
The selected business process for the SmartHerd system is Livestock Record-Keeping and
Health Management. Its primary purpose is to establish an automated workflow for registering
livestock, tracking daily health metrics, reporting illnesses, and coordinating veterinary care.
This eliminates manual record-keeping errors, prevents delayed treatments, and provides reliable
data for daily farm operations and management decision-making.
2. Actors and Responsibilities
 Farmer: Initiates the workflow by registering animals, logging routine health
observations, submitting service requests for sick livestock, and updating general herd
records.
 SmartHerd System (Database): Acts as the automated core that validates user inputs,
stores records in relational tables, evaluates health flags, and sends automated alerts to
veterinarians.
 Veterinarian: Reviews health notifications, assesses reported cases, determines if a
physical visit is needed, and logs diagnoses and prescriptions back into the system.
3. Process Flow & Database Operations
1. Data Creation: The farmer logs livestock or health data into the system. The system
validates the input and inserts new records into the database.
2. Decision & Notification: A decision gateway checks if a health issue is flagged. If yes,
the system automatically notifies the veterinarian.
3. Assessment & Update: The veterinarian retrieves the animal's history, assesses the
condition, and conducts a farm visit if required. The veterinarian then updates the
treatment and prescription records in the database, closing the workflow.
